<%# Fuime: who the buyer is actually contracting with.

    This is not decoration and it is not a disclaimer. Under
    FEATURE_MERCHANT_OF_RECORD the entire legal basis for customer money landing
    in Fuime's own Stripe balance is that Fuime IS the seller — Fuime's terms of
    sale, Fuime's name on the receipt, Fuime carrying the refund and chargeback
    obligation. That is a fact about the commercial relationship, and a fact the
    BUYER has to be able to see.

    Until 2026-08-19 the seller-of-record claim appeared only in operator-facing
    and admin copy. Every screen that said "Fuime LLC is the seller of record"
    faced an operator or an admin; the customer handing over money was told
    nothing. The claim was therefore asserted everywhere except to the one party
    it is about. See docs/fuime/MOR_RISK_ACCEPTANCE.md §2 Q1.

    Rendered only under merchant-of-record. Under Connect the guardian's own
    connected account is the merchant and this would be false.

    Local `event` is the venture fulfilling the order. %>
<% if ::Fuime::Features.merchant_of_record? %>
  <p class="text-sm muted mt-3 mb-0">
    Sold by <strong>Fuime LLC</strong> · fulfilled by <%= event.name %>.
    Fuime handles payment, receipts and refunds —
    <%= link_to "terms of sale", terms_path %>.
  </p>
<% end %>
